Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Scratch work of Author", "Title",
  FontSize->24],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["Patrick L. Nash, Ph.D.",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["\n",
  FontSize->18,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["(c) 2022, under GPL\nProfessor, UTSA Physics and Astronomy, \
Retired (USA)\nPatrick299Nash  at    gmail   ...\nDo not read if you are \
irascible.\ngit clone \
https://github.com/43d168f3e/Eternal-DEFLATION-Inflation.git\n\
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]git@github.com:43d168f3e/Eternal-DEFLATION-Inflation.\
git\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\n\n\nEver wonder why there are  3 space \
dimensions and  1  time dimension?  \nEver wonder if   Nature  loves  the \
norm  relation \:2016XY\:2016 = \:2016X\:2016\:2016Y\:2016, for  X, Y \
\[Element] Nature?\n\nWell, Hurwitz\[CloseCurlyQuote]s theorem  says  that  \
there  are  only  4 normed division algebras (\:2016XY\:2016=\:2016X\:2016\
\:2016Y\:2016) over the real numbers, which, up to isomorphism,  are   the  \
1-dim (over \[DoubleStruckCapitalR]) real numbers  \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR],the   2-dim  complex numbers,the   4-dim   \
quaternions, and the  8-dim   octonions.\n\nThe origin of this calculation \
has its roots in \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]A Remarkable Representation of the \
3+2 de Sitter Group\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] by P.A.M.Dirac, J.Math.Phys.4,901\
\[Dash]909 (1963). \nOf course P.A.M.Dirac has no blame for this use of his \
ideas.\n\nHere, Dirac\[CloseCurlyQuote]s gamma matrices have been extended \
into  this paper\[CloseCurlyQuote]s  real   8\[Cross]8  matrices and  tau16  \
real  16\[Cross]16 matrices.\n\nHere we use ",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["spacetime coordinates",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.4, 0.6, 1]],
 StyleBox[" that are selected so that we are somewhat consistent with the \n",
  
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["xact libraries",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.14, 0.8, 0.14]],
 StyleBox[",\n(which we employ, in other included notebooks, in order to \
calculate the Einstein-Lovelock tensors):\n",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["Cartestian coordinates:\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.4, 0.6, 1],
  Background->None],
 StyleBox["  ",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["x0",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.93, 0.27, 0.27]],
 StyleBox[" = time coord;  \n  ",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["x1, x2, x3",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.93, 0.27, 0.27]],
 StyleBox["  are the usual 3-space coords; \nand  ",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["x4",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.93, 0.27, 0.27]],
 StyleBox[",",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["x5, x6, x7",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.93, 0.27, 0.27]],
 StyleBox["=  extra space coords, for octonions.\n\nThis notebook is \
distributed as free software under the GNU General Public License.They are \
distributed in the hope that they will  be useful,but WITHOUT ANY \
WARRANTY;without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR \
A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.See the GNU GPL for more details.\n\nPlease  cite  this  \
work  and this web page if you use it.\n",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]]
}], "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8726702134099073`*^9, 3.872670317841343*^9}, {
